schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: Gitcoin Grants has distributed $67M+ to 5,000+ projects; GG24 included a $100K Bioregional Reforestation round
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    Gitcoin Grants, the largest quadratic-funding deployment, has helped
    distribute over $67 million to more than 5,000 projects, and its 2025
    round (GG24) included a Bioregional Reforestation round with a $100K
    matching pool split across nine bioregions, including Kenya/Uganda and
    Nigeria.
  evidence: >-
    Cited to "Gitcoin Quadratic Funding" (gitcoin.co/mechanisms/quadratic-
    funding) and "Gitcoin Grants 24" (grants.gitcoin.co) in the article's
    References.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/why-local-matters.md
  interpretation: >-
    Used to support the claim that a small node with no rich donor can still
    draw meaningful matched funding, because quadratic funding rewards breadth
    of backers over size of any single donation.
  uncertainty: >-
    Cumulative platform totals ($67M+/5,000+ projects) are a moving target that
    will be understated over time; the GG24 $100K Bioregional Reforestation
    figure is specific to a named round and should be checked against Gitcoin's
    own round page for current/final numbers rather than treated as a
    standing, repeatable figure.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/why-local-matters.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
